    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with a lineup anchored by **Christian Yelich**, our top-scoring asset at 75.84. He draws a highly favorable matchup against Feltner, whose 4.93 xERA provides the ideal environment for **Christian Yelich** to capitalize on his 13% dynamic platoon edge. We are also tracking **Junior Caminero** (69.49) and **Colt Keith** (68.51) as high-leverage starts. **Junior Caminero** remains a priority despite a slight park penalty, as his elite .376 xwOBA makes him a core contributor, while **Colt Keith** benefits from leading off against Wacha, maximizing his opportunities to accumulate R and SB, our most critical categories.\n\nManaging our efficiency floor was paramount today, leading to the decision to bench **Josh Smith** (45.38). While **Josh Smith** boasts a strong 14% platoon advantage against Woo, his baseline efficiency remains inferior to the combined production potential of our starting core, particularly when accounting for the lineup spots assigned to **Chase Meidroth** and **Casey Schmitt**. We are cautiously optimistic about **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.30) and **Trea Turner** (58.46) despite facing elite arms in Skenes and Weathers; the aggressive SB upside these two provide forces them into the starting lineup regardless of their respective SP Skill penalties. \n\nRisks remain, specifically the negative impact of high-tier opposing pitching on **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Carson Benge**. **Carson Benge** represents our lowest-scoring starter at 46.38 against Yamamoto, and he remains a primary candidate to be pulled if we find ourselves struggling to maintain our daily game cap management. While we are holding **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Hyeseong Kim** on the bench due to either difficult matchups or minor league assignments, the roster is positioned to prioritize stolen base potential and efficient ABs as we push through the mid-summer stretch.",
